+# Column 606 inspection and photograph leads
+
+Public derivative of the November 10, 2026 source review · STL02–STL03 / AUD011 / B188 / H005. Two federal publications reproduce a dated LERA inspection table identifying Column 606 in the installed Tower A structure. A later table names inspection photographs by number. The inspection evidence gives a second way to check the intended location identified in the drawing and the photographed fabrication mark. The photograph, drawing, inspection table and salvage inventory each answer different questions. [1993 inspection table, NCSTAR 1-1C vol. 2, PDF p. 186](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada.pdf#page=186) · [Drawing, PDF p. 19](https://archive.org/download/WTCI000013L/WTCI-000013-L.PDF#page=19) · [Berkeley photograph, PDF p. 3](https://digicoll.lib.berkeley.edu/record/291574/files/504-WTC-Astaneh-a-photo-of-steel-member-with-identification-number-October-2001.pdf#page=3)
+
+## Observations and conflicting readings
+
+| Record | What the source records |
+| --- | --- |
+| **29 January 1993 LERA inspection, P1103904 & 3927**, internal p. 6 of 9 | Both table images show `A (1 WTC) / 21 / 4-78 / 606 / East`. The next row shows `4-78 / 607 / West`. Vol. 2 PDF p. 186 sorted text lines 20–21 instead give `4-73` twice. The NCSTAR 1-6A copy, physical p. 283, sorted lines 17–18, gives `4-78` twice. Preserve all four readings and the shared internal report identity. [Vol. 2 image and text](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada.pdf#page=186) · [1-6A copy](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-fe402b24dd54ccb5e1fc61e65aaa7278/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-fe402b24dd54ccb5e1fc61e65aaa7278.pdf#page=283) |
+| **Same report**, internal pp. 1, 5 and 7 | The executive summary describes the inspected columns as free of structural deficiencies such as cracking or bowing and describes missing fireproofing and light rust. The procedure describes observation from elevator cars and occasional photography when defects were observed. The observation on p. 7 says large areas of fireproofing were missing on Columns 606 and 607, without assigning the affected area to a specific floor interval. The general method and finding are distinct from a measurement of the photographed piece. [1-6A, PDF pp. 281–284](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-fe402b24dd54ccb5e1fc61e65aaa7278/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-fe402b24dd54ccb5e1fc61e65aaa7278.pdf#page=281) |
+| **14 April 1995 LERA inspected-column table**, vol. 2 PDF p. 187 | The image shows `19A / 606 / 2-78, B2 / WEST / 20, -` and `20A / 606 / B2 / EAST & NORTH / 31`. The commas here separate stacked entries. In the sorted text, lines 52–55 include `ISA 606 2-78 ifSST 20`, `B2` and `2 OA 606 32 EAST & NORTH 3 2`. The photo identifiers 20 and 31 are specific retrieval leads. The table alone does not locate photo 20 at floors 48–51. [1995 table](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada.pdf#page=187) |
+| **1996, 1997 and 1998 lists headed Previously Inspected**, vol. 2 PDF pp. 193, 200 and 209 | All three images show `19A / 606 / B2/2-78 / West`. For `20A / 606 / B2/4-78`, the 1996 and 1997 images read `East & North`, and 1998 reads `North & East`. The 20A text rows separately read `20A 505 B2/4-78 East & North` on p. 193 line 22, `20A 606 B2/4-78 East & North` on p. 200 line 44, and `20A 605 BZ'4-78 North & East` on p. 209 line 36. The 1996 image date is 17 May 1996, while p. 193 sorted text line 5 yields `17 May 1S95`. These reproduced inventories describe prior scope. Fresh inspection dates and conditions for each listed entry would require the underlying field reports. [1996 list](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada.pdf#page=193) · [1997 list](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada.pdf#page=200) · [1998 list](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada.pdf#page=209) |
+
+The four combinations of floors 48 and 51 with the two 1993 endpoints, 73 and 78, all fall in the stated inspection ranges. This establishes a range overlap under either reading. It leaves the photograph's face, installed piece identity, location of any missing fireproofing and pre-collapse condition at the photographed segment open. The inspection report's location and condition statements are distinct from a post-collapse piece identification.
+
+## Routing and preservation
+
+NCSTAR 1-1C Table 3–14 identifies the 1993 and 1995 source records as `4078/66-L` and `4079/66-L` and reports routine repair recommendations for both. Its discussion says the Port Authority reported losing construction records on repairs following inspections. The statement describes reported record loss and does not establish the decision or repair history of any specific face or floor. [Table 3–14, PDF p. 120 lines 7–17](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-cb8070ff48f9b1dafa42bd5cbaae0205/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-cb8070ff48f9b1dafa42bd5cbaae0205.pdf#page=120) · [NIST discussion, PDF p. 135 lines 41–49](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-cb8070ff48f9b1dafa42bd5cbaae0205/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-cb8070ff48f9b1dafa42bd5cbaae0205.pdf#page=135)
+
+The tested archive candidate `WTCI000066L` returned HTTP 200 with a two-byte empty metadata object and HTTP 404 at the item page. These outcomes apply to that candidate address. The direct NIST body attempts hit the local byte cap and produced no saved bodies. The GovInfo alternates provided a 220-page volume preserved in full and a 328-page volume read in memory with a verified four-page excerpt. Parent and excerpt hashes are recorded separately. The 1993 table appears in both editions with different page rasters. Both reproduce the same dated LERA table and should be treated as related sources. [GovInfo vol. 2](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-bffc2781d34258d215e5feb86d2b9ada.pdf) · [GovInfo 1-6A](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-fe402b24dd54ccb5e1fc61e65aaa7278/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-fe402b24dd54ccb5e1fc61e65aaa7278.pdf)
+
+## Open tests
+
+- Recover the complete `WTCI-66-L` inspection package, including the 1993 report and appendices and the 1995 report's photos 20 and 31 with captions or field notes. Compare any photographs on face, floor, geometry and distinctive features. The inspected pages identify photo numbers and a source series. A floor-specific photograph and installation or erection documentation are still needed for a piece-level comparison.
+- Seek a contemporaneous 606A as-built or shop record and the repair ticket, clearance or later floor-specific inspection. For salvage identity, the remaining targets are original October 2001 photo metadata and field notes, stamped-piece measurements or end views, and yard dispatch, transfer, intake and disposition records that carry the piece mark or a defensible cross-reference.
+- Carry forward the separate W14A and W14B candidate attribution and C-90 caption and span discrepancies. The Tower A inspection and drawing cannot establish the origin of those items or their record-handling history.
+
+The review checked the cited embedded inspection pages visually, compared their text layers, and reproduced the endpoint inclusion calculation. It did not recover a post-collapse custody record or an NIST accession for the photographed member.
